{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XSS3xDkwiZXyaFUJHEVc1h","type":"tool_result","content":"298:lemma IsTree.card_edgeFinset [Fintype V] [Fintype G.edgeSet] (hG : G.IsTree) :\n477:  rw [Nat.card_eq_fintype_card, ← hT.card_edgeFinset, add_le_add_iff_right,\n486:  refine ⟨fun h ↦ ⟨h.connected, by simpa [edgeFinset] using h.card_edgeFinset⟩,\n499:  · have := h.card_edgeFinset\n---PD\n29:structure PathDecomposition (G : SimpleGraph V) where\n30-  /-- Number of bags minus 1 (so there are `length + 1` bags). -/\n31-  length : ℕ\n32-  /-- The bag function mapping indices to sets of vertices. -/\n33-  bag : Fin (length + 1) → Finset V\n34-  /-- Every vertex appears in at least one bag. -/\n35-  vertex_coverage : ∀ v : V, ∃ i, v ∈ bag i\n36-  /-- Both endpoints of every edge appear together in some bag. -/\n37-  edge_coverage : ∀ u v : V, G.Adj u v → ∃ i, u ∈ bag i ∧ v ∈ bag i\n38-  /-- The bags containing any vertex form a contiguous interval. -/\n39-  interval : ∀ (v : V) (i j k : Fin (length + 1)),\n40-    i ≤ j → j ≤ k → v ∈ bag i → v ∈ bag k → v ∈ bag j\n41-\nlean/MOSPFormalization/Pathwidth.lean:21:noncomputable def pathwidth : ℕ :=\n---SP\n254:inductive SPStep (G : SimpleGraph V) (v : V) : SimpleGraph V → Prop\n255-  /-- Operation 2: `v` has the single neighbour `x`; delete `v`. -/\n256-  | pendant {x : V} (hx : G.Adj v x) (hall : ∀ z, G.Adj v z → z = x) : SPStep G v (isolate G v)\n257-  /-- Operation 3: `v` has exactly the two non-adjacent neighbours `x ≠ y`; delete `v` and\n258-  add the edge `xy`. -/\n259-  | suppress {x y : V} (hx : G.Adj v x) (hy : G.Adj v y) (hxy : x ≠ y)\n260-      (hall : ∀ z, G.Adj v z → z = x ∨ z = y) (hnadj : ¬ G.Adj x y) :\n261-      SPStep G v (isolate G v ⊔ SimpleGraph.edge x y)\n262-  /-- Operation 4: `v` has exactly the two adjacent neighbours `x ≠ y`; delete `v`. -/\n263-  | triangle {x y : V} (hx : G.Adj v x) (hy : G.Adj v y) (hxy : x ≠ y)\n264-      (hall : ∀ z, G.Adj v z → z = x ∨ z = y) (hadj : G.Adj x y) : SPStep G v (isolate G v)\n265-\n266-/-- The reflexive–transitive closure of \"some step\". `SPReduces G ⊥` is the paper's\n267-\"`r(G)` is empty\". -/\n268-def SPReduces (G H : SimpleGraph V) : Prop :=\n269-  Relation.ReflTransGen (fun G H => ∃ v, SPStep G v H) G H\n270-\n271-/-- Every degree is `0` or at least `3`: no operation applies. -/\n272-def IsSPReduced (G : SimpleGraph V) : Prop := ∀ v, ndeg G v = 0 ∨ 3 ≤ ndeg G v\n273-\n274-/-- Basic (paper p. 8): every non-trivial component `C` is cubic, or some `v ∈ C` has\n275-`r((G|C) − v)` empty. -/\n276-def IsBasic (G : SimpleGraph V) : Prop :=\n---MONO\n120:theorem pathwidth_mono {G H : SimpleGraph V} (h : H ≤ G) : pathwidth H ≤ pathwidth G :=\n129:theorem pathwidth_eq_of_iso {W : Type*} [Fintype W] [DecidableEq W]\n154:def isolate (G : SimpleGraph V) (v : V) : SimpleGraph V where\n333:theorem pathwidth_le_of_le_minorOf (G : SimpleGraph V) (seq : List (V × Option V))\n---GENG\nD3 n=8: D3 n=9: D3 n=10: ---PAPER\npaper1/latex/sec9e_appendix_random.tex:598:\\citep[Theorem~5]{FominHoie2006}; the paper gives no constant for either\npaper1/latex/sec9e_appendix_random.tex:610:connected cubic graphs with a budget~$\\tau$ \\citep[Theorem~5]{FominHoie2006},\npaper1/latex/sec9a_appendix_lean.tex:131:  base case \\path{CubicPathwidthBound} with budget $\\tau$ \\citep[Theorem~5]{FominHoie2006} and the\n97:at every `c` (table §7(a)), because no 1/3–2/3 balancing slack is needed for\n253:- **[derived] Critical point `c = 1`:** `pw ≤ (2/3) log₃ n + O(1)`, since the\n254:  components have size `O(n^{2/3})` and bounded excess. `pw → ∞`, since every\n258:  cyclomatic bound, `pw ≤ (2/3 + o(1)) ε³n + O(log n)` [derived], so\n435:| 1 | critical | `pw → ∞`, `≤ (2/3) log₃ n` | derived | — | — | — |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"729a31ea-6900-48bd-999c-66286e063162","uuid":"1b79ab75-c009-4a2d-a0ef-dfebd6843563","timestamp":"2026-11-02T06:58:10.940Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"298:lemma IsTree