his loop.\n\nAlso superseded, in the same file's §3.3: \"closed form not read\" — Lemma 8.1\nis `g_closed_form` in `Weights.lean` (§3).\n\n### 10.5 Edits to §1–§9 for one voice\n\nThe header no longer says §0 \"is written by item 10\"; §9.7's title and its\ntwo forward references now say the rows are in the paper; otherwise §1–§9\nstand as their items wrote them — each already follows the same pattern\n(regenerate, size range, checks, statements, choices beyond the design, axiom\nrecord, kill verdict, what it does not claim), and rewriting them would put\nwords in the record that no check produced.\n\n### 10.6 Kill verdict, and what this does not claim\n\n**Kill verdict: none** (the item has no kill criterion).\n\n**Does not claim.** Anything beyond what items 01–09 proved, measured or\ncited; that the paper's paragraph is final (the owner edits the paper); that\nthe `CLAUDE.md` paragraph is applied (it is drafted here); that the page\ngrowth is the paragraph's (it is three few-line spills); that the survey's\nother upper-bound entries were checked.\n---02\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Brute-force check of every intermediate statement of the Edwards–McDermid\nchain (loop0012 item 02; `reports/edwards_mcdermid.md` §2; the plan is\n`reports/edwards_mcdermid_plan.md` §0.3–0.5) on every graph on 1–9 vertices\nfrom `nauty-geng`, pathwidth by the vertex-separation subset DP.\n\nThe statements, numbered as in the report's §2 (W = weights, C = cut lemma,\nP = potential, R = reduction system, S = step inequality, T = Theorem 3.2,\nA = assembly budgets, B = basic graphs, H = the shape of hypothesis (H3)):\n\n  W1–W5  recurrence, g non-decreasing, g' non-increasing from 3, property 6,\n         0 ≤ g < 1 and 0 ≤ g' ≤ 1/6, the closed form (exact rationals, to n = 40;\n         main process)\n  C1     pw(G) ≤ max(pw(G[V1]) + |∂1|, pw(G[V2]) + |∂2|, |∂1| + |∂2| − 1)\n         (every partition of every graph); C1s the separator form\n         pw(G) ≤ max(pw(G[V1]), pw(G[V2])) + min(|∂1|, |∂2|), and C1s ≤ C1\n  C2     iterated form on a depth-2 bisection: pw(G) ≤ 2 Σ_i b_i + max_leaf pw;\n         C2s the separator form Σ_i b_i + max_leaf pw (b_i the largest\n         min(|∂1|, |∂2|) at level i); random trees\n  R6     one step costs at most one: pw(H) ≤ pw(H') + 1 (every step)\n  P1     f(G − w) = f(G) − g(d(w)) − Σ_{v ∈ N(w)} g'(d(v))        (every w)\n  P2     degrees 0 or ≥ 3, w of maximum degree Δ ≥ 4 with a neighbour of degree\n         ≤ Δ − 1 ⇒ f(G − w) ≤ f(G) − 1; Δ-regular, Δ ≥ 4 ⇒\n         f(G − w) = f(G) − 1 + g'(Δ − 1) − g'(Δ)\n  R1     every SPStep (at a vertex of degree 1 or 2) removes ≥ 1 edge\n  R2     every SPStep lowers no degree-count: deg_{H'}(u) ≤ deg_H(u) for all u,\n         hence f(H') ≤ f(H); a vertex of degree d isolated by the step loses g(d)\n  R3     commutation: SPStep H H' at v, w ≠ v ⇒ H' − w = H − w, or\n         H' − w = SPStep (H − w) at v (with v of degree 1 or 2 in H − w)\n  R5     a step at v inside a component acts on that component only\n  RU     (measured) every maximal reduction order reaches the same reduct\n  S0     the hinge: G* a reduced reduct of G' = G − w, v with d_{G'}(v) = d ≥ 3\n         ⇒ f(G') − f(G*) + g'(δ(G*)) ≥ g'(d)\n  S1     the step inequality for the paper's choice of w; S1′ for every\n         maximum-degree w (measured); both in the global-minimum form\n         1 + f(G*) − g'(δ(G*)) ≤ f(G) − g'(δ(G)), which implies the\n         per-component form 1 + f⁻(G*) ≤ f⁻(G)\n  SJ     the j-identity (paper (2)–(4)): 1 + f(G') = f(G) − j1 − j2 − j3\n  T1     Algorithm X: X, B with B non-empty, reduced, basic,\n         |X| + f⁻(B) ≤ f⁻(G); and (measured) r(G − X) = B\n  A1/A2  the budgets the record needs at n ≤ 9: max of pw − f⁻ over reduced\n         graphs and of pw − main term over all graphs, per n\n  B1     connected, every degree ≥ 3, not cubic ⇒ f⁻ ≥ 5/6; connected cubic ⇒\n         f⁻ = N/6 − 1/6; f⁻(component) ≥ 0; additivity over components\n  H3     pw(G) − pw(r(G)) per n (its maximum is the shape of (H3) at these sizes)\n\nA violation prints the graph6 string and stops (unless --no-stop).\n\n    nice -n 19 python3 reports/scratch/edwards_mcdermid/02_lemmas/check.py --max-n 9 --workers 8\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport collections\nimport json\nimport random\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport time\nfrom fractions import Fraction","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"729a31ea-6900-48bd-999c-66286e063162","uuid":"496b2aba-f397-4a62-99ee-8d133fc17dc9","timestamp":"2026-11-02T06:59:19.098Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"158:theorem pathwidth_le_pathwidth_isolateSet_add_card (G : SimpleGraph V) (X : Finset V) :\n159-    pathwidth G ≤ pathwidth (isolateSet G X) + X.card := by\n160-  have h := pathwidth_le_pathwidth_induce_add_card_compl G Xᶜ\n161-  rw [compl_compl] at h\n151:theorem isolate_eq_self_of_forall_not_adj {G : SimpleGraph V} {v : V} (h : ∀ z, ¬ G.Adj v z) :\n161:theorem isolate_eq_self_of_ndeg_eq_zero {G : SimpleGraph V} {v : V} (h : ndeg G v = 0) :\n180:def isolateSet (G : SimpleGraph V) (X : Finset V) : SimpleGraph V where\n192:theorem isolateSet_le (G : SimpleGraph V) (X : Finset V) : isolateSet G X ≤ G :=\n195:theorem isolateSet_empty (G : SimpleGraph V) : isolateSet G ∅ = G := by\n198:theorem isolateSet_singleton (G : SimpleGraph V) (w : V) : isolateSet G {w} = isolate G w := by\n201:theorem isolateSet_insert (G : SimpleGraph V) (w : V) (X : Finset V) :\n---\n\n/-- The vertices of positive degree (the \"non-removed\" vertices of the design). -/\ndef supp (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : Finset V :=\n  univ.filter (fun v => 0 < G.degree v)\n\ntheorem mem_supp {G : SimpleGraph V} [DecidableRel G.Adj] {v : V} :\n    v ∈ supp G ↔ 0 < G.degree v := by\n  simp [supp]\n\ntheorem mem_supp_iff_exists_adj {G : SimpleGraph V} [DecidableRel G.Adj] {v : V} :\n    v ∈ supp G ↔ ∃ w, G.Adj v w := by\n  rw [mem_supp, G.degree_pos_iff_exists_adj]\n\ninstance instDecida